"coverage\"","\"display\"","\"factor_contributions\"","\"final\"","\"known_contribution\"","\"missing_weight\"","\"post_cap_bounds\"","\"pre_cap_bounds\"","\"raw\"","\"weights\"","\"3.5\"","\"5.7\"","\"0.76\"","\"NS\"","\"BAL\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"DUR\"","\"EXEC\"","\"GOV\"","\"MOAT\"","\"REV\"","\"score\"","\"weight\"","\"weighted_contribution\"","6","\"0.48\"","\"0.50\"","\"0.32\"","\"0.80\"","\"3.30\"","\"0.24\"","\"3.54\"","\"5.70\"","\"2.1\"","\"8.4\"","\"EARN\"","\"1.00\"","\"1.40\"","\"0.70\"","\"2.10\"","\"8.40\"","\"1.4\"","\"8.6\"","\"D\"","\"L\"","\"P\"","\"Q\"","\"R\"","\"0.60\"","\"0.35\"","\"8.60\"","\"-1\"","\"1\"","\"BQS_bound\"","\"BQS_final\"","\"GQS_final\"","\"IAS_effect_if_all_else_complete\"","\"IAS_final\"","\"hypothetical_factor\"","\"3.46\"","\"5.62\"","\"NS unchanged\"","\"-0.0200\"","\"NS unchanged because Q remains incomplete and gates hold\"","\"3.62\"","\"5.78\"","\"0.0200\"","7","\"3.34\"","\"5.50\"","\"-0.0500\"","\"3.74\"","\"5.90\"","\"0.0500\"","\"confidence\"","\"contrary_fact\"","\"evidence_ids\"","\"Medium\"","\"Low audited debt is real, but stale cash, opening liability settlements and uncertain facility availability limit its protection.\"","\"E05\"","\"E06\"","\"E14\"","\"E16\"","\"E20\"","\"E21\"","\"Audited net cash and equity-funded expansion, subject to stale entry cash, claim settlement and intraperiod shortfall risks.\"","\"Low\"","\"The Covid-base five-year proxy looks strong and CWIP may mature; neither resolves current asset/provision classifications or negative three-year incremental proxy.\"","\"E08\"","\"E24\"","\"E25\"","\"Broad incremental-return proxy deteriorates, but provision classification, doubtful AR, asset maturity and harmonized IC are material unresolved denominators; do not force a point score.\"","\"Five-year reported CFO/PAT is0.77, and FY23 cash generation was strong; recent FCF and liability-supported FY26CFO are contrary evidence.\"","\"E02\"","\"E04\"","\"Audited ratio-of-sums plus persistent working-capital demands and recent negative FCF; FY26 provision-normalized conversion is worse, not a capex excuse for CFO.\"","\"March net cash and repeat demand provide protection; they do not prevent collection/capex timing stress or SME exit constraints.\"","\"E03\"","\"E18\"","\"Limited cash buffer under collection/capex stress, dilution and concentrated exit liquidity; not a price-derived favorable downside claim.\"","\"Consumables recur across uses, but export contraction and concentrated customers can impair recurrence.\"","\"E07\"","\"E10\"","\"E19\"","\"Recurring consumables across fabrication/repair sectors, offset industrial cyclicality, top-ten concentration and export collapse.\"","\"Reported PAT rose in FY26; that does not resolve doubtful allowance or establish normalized recurring earnings growth.\"","\"E15\"","\"Other income, allowance inconsistency, legacy restatement and unusual provisions prevent reliable organic normalized earnings-growth score.\"","\"Expansion, solar and lower remuneration are positive execution evidence; measured utilization/payback and export continuity do not yet confirm it.\"","\"E11\"","\"Capacity/solar investment and lower remuneration are positives, but export contraction and lower incremental returns; utilization and commissioning outcomes unverified.\"","\"Director loans were repaid by FY23 and AS15 was restated; lower remuneration and later compliance wording mitigate the historical findings.\"","\"E12\"","\"E13\"","\"Three years of Section185 director-loan contraventions, repaid by FY23; later wording reports compliance but FY25 RPT loan direction is contradictory. Historical and current reliability issues require a hold, not an unproven diversion allegation.\"","\"Observed trading and a19200-share latest session show some activity; missing sessions, lot size and absent live depth prevent executable liquidity scoring.\"","\"21 missing security rows are not verified zero-volume days; no contemporaneous depth/circuit restriction evidence, and whole-lot participation fails observed-only diagnostics.\"","\"Approvals and repeat consumable demand plausibly create customer friction; no quantified premium or exclusivity was found.\"","\"E23\"","\"Qualified consumables and repeat orders, but no verified durable price premium, margin persistence, market share or switching-cost economics.\"","\"Trailing18.18xPAT can look moderate; reliable normalized capital/cash and intrinsic-value support remain unavailable.\"","\"E17\"","\"E22\"","\"No reliable conservative intrinsic-value margin of safety while G2 remains on hold.\"","\"Some bull paths survive without finance and reach break-even, but current evidence holds and hurdle tests prevent an investable point score.\"","\"Conditional modeled returns cannot cure financial-reliability and entry-cash gaps.\"","\"FY26 nominal revenue grew14.04%, but value added was nearly flat and current unit/price decomposition is missing.\"","\"E09\"","\"Nominal audited growth is calculable but latest volume/price/mix bridge and commodity-adjusted economic growth cannot be established.\"","\"G1\"","\"G2\"","\"G3\"","\"G4\"","\"Repeated historical statutory loan violations are evidenced. Year-end repayment and later compliance language mitigate, but FY25 loan-direction and control-resolution gaps remain. Present severe diversion/minority harm is not proven.\"","\"Conditional\"","\"₹2.9709cr doubtful AR with nil allowance; ₹4.2034cr unexplained other provisions; contradictory CARO investment and contingency disclosures. Obtain ledger, collections, settlement and auditor reconciliations.\"","\"Hold — unresolved\"","\"Low audited debt, but March cash is not October cash, provisions and capex consume funds. Cash models are conditional and rescue is uncommitted; no verified current default.\"","\"Stale last observed trade and incomplete security-row coverage; observed-only ₹5lakh test is not executable and does not establish an actual 60-day exit.\"","\"Decimal 